  "notes": "どこか is an indefinite word meaning \"somewhere\" or \"somehow.\" Part of the ka-series indefinites.\n\nTWO MAIN USES:\n1. Location (somewhere): どこかに{行|い}く (go somewhere)\n2. Manner (somehow, somewhat): どこか{変|へん}だ (somehow strange)\n\nPARTICLE PATTERNS:\n- どこかに: to/at somewhere\n- どこかで: at somewhere (action location)\n- どこかへ: toward somewhere\n\nRELATED INDEFINITES:\n- {何|なに}か: something\n- {誰|だれ}か: someone\n- いつか: sometime\n- どれか: one of them\n\nUSAGE NOTE:\nWhen modifying an adjective without a particle, どこか means \"somewhat\" or \"in some way\": どこか{寂|さび}しい (somehow lonely).",
